  "id": "COMPOUND:38301 - PROTEIN:5792",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Hedaol B and RWLeu4, mediated through the compound (1S,3R,6S,8R,11S,12S,15R,16R)-15-[(2R)-4-[(2R)-3,3-dimethyloxiran-2-yl]butan-2-yl]-7,7,12,16-tetramethylpentacyclo[9.7.0.01,3.03,8.012,16]octadecan-6-ol. This compound is identified as a target of Hedaol B in multiple contexts, including HepG2 and A549 cell lines, and it directly targets RWLeu4. The consistent presence of this compound in the target list across different cell lines indicates a possible mechanism of action involving RWLeu4. The evidence suggests that Hedaol B may inhibit RWLeu4 through direct interaction, possibly by binding to it or modulating its activity. The presence of this compound in multiple contexts also implies a potential role in cellular processes that could be relevant to disease states. The integration of these findings supports a mechanistic link between Hedaol B and RWLeu4, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact nature of the interaction.",
